ATEMENT OF THE CAPTAIN. (1849.)"},{"id":"s55","label":"Ch. 3","title":"THE STATEMENT OF MR. MURTHWAITE. (1850.)"}],"groups":[{"id":"g-ablewhite","label":"Ablewhite (shared surname)"},{"id":"g-verinder","label":"Verinder (shared surname)"},{"id":"g-betteredge","label":"Betteredge (shared surname)"}],"characters":[{"id":"franklin-blake","name":"Franklin Blake","aliases":["Mr. Franklin","Mr. Blake","Mr. Franklin Blake","Franklin"],"role":"protagonist","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: “Only this morning (May twenty-first, eighteen hundred and fifty), came my lady’s nephew, Mr.”"},{"id":"sergeant-cuff","name":"Sergeant Cuff","aliases":["Cuff"],"role":"major","firstAppearance":"s15","summary":"First mention: “The name of him was Sergeant Cuff; and the arrival of him from London might be expected by the morning train.”"},{"id":"rachel","name":"Rachel","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s6","summary":"First mention: “He has been staying with his father in London, and he is coming to us tomorrow to stop till next month, and keep Rachel’s birthday.””"},{"id":"rosanna-spearman","name":"Rosanna Spearman","aliases":["Rosanna"],"role":"major","firstAppearance":"s7","summary":"First mention: ““Rosanna’s late again for dinner,” says Nancy.”"},{"id":"sergeant","name":"Sergeant","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s15","summary":"First mention: “Superintendent Seegrave, returning to us at his appointed time, and hearing that the Sergeant was expected, instantly shut himself up in a room, with pen, ink, and paper, to make notes of the Report which would be cer…”"},{"id":"mr-bruff","name":"Mr. Bruff","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: “Mr.”"},{"id":"miss-rachel","name":"Miss Rachel","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “Shortly afterwards Sir John died, and my lady was left with her little girl, Miss Rachel, and no other child.”"},{"id":"godfrey-ablewhite","name":"Godfrey Ablewhite","aliases":["Mr. Godfrey","Mr. Godfrey Ablewhite"],"role":"major","group":"g-ablewhite","firstAppearance":"s11","summary":"First mention: “His name was Mr.”"},{"id":"miss-verinder","name":"Miss Verinder","role":"major","group":"g-verinder","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: ““Tell Colonel Herncastle,” she said, when I gave her her brother’s message, “that Miss Verinder is engaged, and that _I_ decline to see him.”"},{"id":"moonstone","name":"Moonstone","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “The deity commanded that the Moonstone should be watched, from that time forth, by three priests in turn, night and day, to the end of the generations of men.”"},{"id":"penelope","name":"Penelope","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “I was left with my little girl Penelope, and with no other child.”"},{"id":"mr-luker","name":"Mr. Luker","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s26","summary":"First mention: “Besides the annoyance complained of, Mr.”"},{"id":"indians","name":"Indians","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “I got to an open door, and saw the bodies of two Indians (by their dress, as I guessed, officers of the palace) lying across the entrance, dead.”"},{"id":"mr-candy","name":"Mr. Candy","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s13","summary":"First mention: “The guest on her left was Mr.”"},{"id":"ezra-jennings","name":"Ezra Jennings","aliases":["Mr. Jennings"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s41","summary":"First mention: ““Ezra Jennings.””"},{"id":"lady-verinder","name":"Lady Verinder","role":"supporting","group":"g-verinder","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “_The Events related by Gabriel Betteredge, house-steward in the service of Julia, Lady Verinder._”"},{"id":"mr-betteredge","name":"Mr. Betteredge","role":"supporting","group":"g-betteredge","firstAppearance":"s7","summary":"First mention: “Let me alone, Mr.”"},{"id":"superintendent-seegrave","name":"Superintendent Seegrave","aliases":["Mr. Superintendent","Mr. Seegrave","Superintendent"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s14","summary":"First mention: “Superintendent Seegrave, of your local police force, and two of his men.”"},{"id":"miss-clack","name":"Miss Clack","aliases":["Clack"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s26","summary":"First mention: “Certain speculations followed, referring to a poor relation of the family—one Miss Clack, whom I have mentioned in my account of the birthday dinner, as sitting next to Mr.”"},{"id":"colonel","name":"Colonel","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: ““The wicked Colonel’s will has left his Diamond as a birthday present to my cousin Rachel,” says Mr.”"},{"id":"mr-ablewhite","name":"Mr. Ablewhite","role":"supporting","group":"g-ablewhite","firstAppearance":"s11","summary":"First mention: “There was terrible work in the family when the Honourable Caroline insisted on marrying plain Mr.”"},{"id":"godfrey","name":"Godfrey","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s12","summary":"First mention: “Could I tell him where his cousin Godfrey was?”"},{"id":"mr-murthwaite","name":"Mr. Murthwaite","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s13","summary":"First mention: “The other guest, who sat on my young lady’s right hand, was an eminent public character—being no other than the celebrated Indian traveller, Mr.”"},{"id":"gooseberry","name":"Gooseberry","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s48","summary":"First mention: ““They call the poor little wretch ‘Gooseberry’ at the office,” he said.”"},{"id":"mrs-yolland","name":"Mrs. Yolland","aliases":["Yolland"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s18","summary":"First mention: “On the Sergeant describing the place, I recognised it as a cottage inhabited by a fisherman named Yolland, with his wife and two grown-up children, a son and a daughter.”"},{"id":"mrs-merridew","name":"Mrs. Merridew","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s38","summary":"First mention: “She was living under the care of a widowed sister of the late Sir John Verinder—one Mrs.”"},{"id":"samuel","name":"Samuel","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s10","summary":"First mention: “Towards midnight, I went round the house to lock up, accompanied by my second in command (Samuel, the footman), as usual.”"},{"id":"gabriel-betteredge","name":"Gabriel Betteredge","role":"minor","group":"g-betteredge","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “_The Events related by Gabriel Betteredge, house-steward in the service of Julia, Lady Verinder._”"},{"id":"sir-john","name":"Sir John","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: ““Sir John,” she says, “I can’t do without Gabriel Betteredge.”"},{"id":"herncastle","name":"Herncastle","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “A foolish wrangle followed; and Herncastle’s unlucky temper got the better of him.”"},{"id":"hindoo","name":"Hindoo","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “At that date, the Mohammedan conqueror, Mahmoud of Ghizni, crossed India; seized on the holy city of Somnauth; and stripped of its treasures the famous temple, which had stood for centuries—the shrine of Hindoo pilgri…”"},{"id":"limping-lucy","name":"Limping Lucy","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s18","summary":"First mention: “Rosanna’s acquaintance with them had begun by means of the daughter, who was afflicted with a misshapen foot, and who was known in our parts by the name of Limping Lucy.”"}],"relationships":[{"id":"r1","source":"herncastle","target":"moonstone","weight":4,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":1,"note":"First named together in Ch. 2."}]},{"id":"r2","source":"indians","target":"moonstone","weight":40,"phases":[{"at":"s2","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":1,"note":"First named together in Ch. 3."},{"at":"s21","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":12},{"at":"s55","type":"together","label":"Constantly together","wei